#: includes/abilities/emails/edit-email.php:63
msgid "Change part of an email instead of rewriting the whole body with groundhogg/update-email-template. For an email built with the block editor: find and replace text, or change, add, move and delete blocks by id. Get the block ids from groundhogg/get-email-template (its outline), and read only the blocks you need to change with its `blocks` input. For an email that isn't built with blocks, like one from the HTML editor: \"replace_text\" for visible text, and \"replace_html\" for an exact piece of the HTML (links, styles, images, rows), which groundhogg/get-email-template's `find` returns to copy. Operations are applied in order, all or nothing, and every change is checked so the email still opens in the editor. Use groundhogg/update-email-template for the subject, sender, status and other settings."
msgstr ""

