msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/emails/edit-email.php:81
msgid "Check the operations and describe the result without saving it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/emails/edit-email.php:94
msgid "\"replace_text\": `find` and `replace`, optionally only in `block`; the cheapest way to change wording or a link. It must match exactly once unless `all` is true. It matches the HTML as written, so text split by tags like <strong> won't match. Matching text in the block settings (like a button's) is changed too. In an email that isn't built with blocks it only matches visible text, not tags, attributes or CSS. \"replace_html\", only for emails that aren't built with blocks: `find` and `replace`, an exact piece of the HTML and what to put in its place, like an href=\"...\" or a whole <tr>...</tr>; it must match exactly once unless `all` is true, and tags it opens must be closed. \"set_content\": `block` and `html`, the new HTML inside the block's <td>; the <td> (padding, background) and settings stay. \"set_props\": `block` and `props`, changes only the given settings in the block's comment, null removes one; the email's HTML isn't rebuilt from them, so this is for settings used when sending (like include_filters or a global block's templateId) or only when editing. \"add\": `blocks` (specs) or `html` with one or more new blocks, and `at`. \"replace\": `block`, and `blocks` or `html` with the blocks to put in its place; ids of the blocks being replaced can be reused. \"move\": `block` and `at`, it moves with the blocks inside it. \"delete\": `block`, and the blocks inside it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/emails/edit-email.php:106
msgid "For \"replace_text\" and \"replace_html\": replace every match instead of needing exactly one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/emails/edit-email.php:115
